{"type":"record","id":"ec7756c0-cd14-11f1-b7c1-47b553663159","topic":"forward-register-topic-register","sender":"Theta","timestamp":"2026-10-21T06:01:57.548Z","text":"Hand-off: CHAT-jmnjvupr\nState:      Stage 1 merged as PR #259. Stage 2 merged as PR #262 at bb0796d3. Stage 3 tasks 1 to 6 are committed on branch worktree-chat-jmnjvupr-stage-3 at 914d96ca, base 103e9547. The branch is not pushed. No PR is open. Task 7 items 1 to 9 are done. The six in-progress issues have topics, and every agent is a member of each.\nLanded:     PR #262, stage 2. It delivered the node-9 launcher, its Compose project, the schema step, image save and load, and the live proof.\nCheckout:   master at bb0796d3, the last substantive merge. A register change does not move this row.\nMerge:      Merge commits only. Every merge needs Mario's explicit authorization and the owner's named --admin bypass. A review comment is not that authorization.\nBranches:   worktree-chat-jmnjvupr-stage-3 holds the stage 3 work in the worktree chat-jmnjvupr-stage-3. chat-hcfgkbuz-node-9 is kept at 1ad85a5e, and its worktree is removed. Every branch ref is kept.\nCoverage:   The coverage table has 26 rows and 0 failures. The read median is under the 10 s target for 7 topics, 8 pointers, 7 entries, and 15 messages. One duplicate-pointer warning comes from the CHAT-live6 test pointers. No denied warning appeared. See docs/superpowers/proofs/2026-10-20-register/COVERAGE.md.\nMeasured:   Stage 2, live. Node 9 started beside node 16 and reported health on 6891. A second start applied no schema. A post wrote a vector without a rebuild. A restart reused the vector files. Toggle off kept the files. Node 16 stayed unchanged. node-9/bin/start calls no Maven when the image is present.\nDecisions:  Design decisions 1 to 38. 36 sets the read warning for a denied topic. 37 sets the owner login. 38 sets the denied-index guard for open and post.\nTraps:      A denied index reads as empty. Use the guard of decision 38. A denied-index or denied-topic warning is a coverage failure. Node 9 runs on 6890 and 6891. chat-deploy core controls node 16, so never run it near node 16.\nUnverified: The move to another host, and the owner named no destination. Design items 5 and 7. The native one-shot image builds, and its context does not start. Case A11 is not run. The owner vault node-9/ansible/vault/owner.yml is absent. The shared vault content is unverified. The second-denial branch of decision 38 has offline tests only. The 30 s default limit is covered offline, because the core answers in about 5 s.\nNext:       The wrapper limit check. Then the AGENTS.md switch, which Mario reviews first. The file forward-register.md stays until that review.\nPointers:   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-17-topic-register-design.md, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-topic-register-stage-3.md, docs/SHELL-COMMAND-CONTRACT.md, docs/superpowers/proofs/2026-10-20-register/RECORD.md, fp CHAT-jmnjvupr.\nArchive:    forward-register-archive-2026-08.md, forward-register-archive-2026-09.md, forward-register-archive-2026-10.md, forward-register-archive-2026-10-17.md, forward-register-archive-2026-10-18.md, forward-register-archive-2026-10-19.md.\nIssues:     The in-progress issues are CHAT-aqpcacwv, CHAT-owiksxvz, CHAT-ivtnvgyg, CHAT-uxlstrdy, CHAT-pphwooqm, and CHAT-jmnjvupr.\n"}
{"type":"record","id":"dc3f5700-cd12-11f1-b7c1-47b553663159","topic":"forward-register-durable-deployment","sender":"Theta","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:47:11.344Z","text":"Hand-off: CHAT-aqpcacwv\nState:      In progress. The durable deployment ran on 2026-10-16 with just deploy-core-cassandra-lucene-redis 16 --key-type uuid. Health is UP on 6791, and Consul lists core-service-rsocket as passing. Keyspace chat_uuid was created fresh, and chat_long is kept.\nDecisions:  The owner set the shape on 2026-10-04. Cassandra is the durable store. Redis carries live pub/sub only. Lucene holds file indexes. REST serves more than one agent. Optional MCP messaging is CHAT-teujorxl.\nTraps:      Vector indexing of imports is out of this deployment. CHAT-dteylnje holds that work.\nUnverified: Scenario 1 is not run. It imports a claude.ai export, then reads it in chat-shell.\nNext:       Run scenario 1 as Admin, then read the log in chat-shell.\nPointers:   fp CHAT-aqpcacwv, CHAT-dteylnje, CHAT-teujorxl.\n"}
{"type":"record","id":"f2111ff0-cd12-11f1-b7c1-47b553663159","topic":"forward-register-toolchain","sender":"Theta","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:47:47.951Z","text":"Hand-off: CHAT-owiksxvz\nState:      In progress. master holds Java 25, Kotlin 2.4.10, Spring Boot 3.5.16, Spring Cloud 2025.0.3, and Spring AI 1.0.3. PR #63 wave 1, PR #64 Kotlin 2.4.10, and PR #65 JDK 25 are merged. The last measured state is 2026-09-06.\nDecisions:  Boot 4 and Spring AI 2.0 form a parallel track. They do not block the current line.\nTraps:      The issue description holds stale versions. The forward register carried the current numbers.\nUnverified: The open children are CHAT-feodvffh, CHAT-eroapfub, CHAT-hvactuvm, CHAT-ixazwico, CHAT-gidbchkx, CHAT-incuynpc, CHAT-pkolwuqm, and CHAT-ygllyglb. Their state is older than 2026-09-06.\nNext:       Read fp CHAT-owiksxvz before any work on this topic.\nPointers:   fp CHAT-owiksxvz, PR #63, PR #64, PR #65.\n"}
{"type":"record","id":"07d0e780-cd13-11f1-b7c1-47b553663159","topic":"forward-register-keytests-codec","sender":"Theta","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:48:24.440Z","text":"Hand-off: CHAT-ivtnvgyg\nState:      Open on purpose. The Jackson 3 codec error on KeyTests from 2026-09-22 stays unrepaired. PR #228 repaired the separate loopback port trap, and it merged as 04dbe77a on 2026-10-15.\nDecisions:  Do not close this issue from the port fix alone.\nTraps:      The issue holds two defects. The port trap is repaired. The codec error is not.\nUnverified: The codec error has no reproduction record newer than 2026-09-22.\nNext:       Reproduce the KeyTests codec error, then read the walk-through in the issue body.\nPointers:   fp CHAT-ivtnvgyg, PR #228, merge 04dbe77a.\n"}
{"type":"record","id":"1d5330e0-cd13-11f1-b7c1-47b553663159","topic":"forward-register-message-capture","sender":"Theta","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:49:00.526Z","text":"Hand-off: CHAT-uxlstrdy\nState:      In progress. The spec is docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-domain-command-bus-design.md. The newest comment is 2026-10-09. Implementation waits for review of the complete spec.\nDecisions:  Owner decisions 1 and 2 are in the spec. Admission assigns the message ID and root with no key registry write. A launch selector chooses the memory or kafka bus.\nTraps:      Three contracts were open at the last review. Group scope must cover local Index state. Case 17 needs a replay or catch-up boundary. Case 7 must separate an aborted admission from a lost acknowledgment.\nUnverified: The spec review is not complete. No implementation started.\nNext:       Read fp CHAT-uxlstrdy and the spec before any work.\nPointers:   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-domain-command-bus-design.md, fp CHAT-uxlstrdy.\n"}
{"type":"record","id":"336b9fc0-cd13-11f1-b7c1-47b553663159","topic":"forward-register-kafka-stage-2","sender":"Theta","timestamp":"2026-10-21T05:49:37.596Z","text":"Hand-off: CHAT-pphwooqm\nState:      In progress. Stage 1 merged in PR #201 as e8d9ed13. Stage 2 is design work. No Stage 2 implementation started.\nDecisions:  The owner clarified scope on 2026-10-09. Stage 2 must not optimize for maximum durability or require multi-node clusters. Preserve the command patterns and a path to stronger durability.\nTraps:      A single replica does not make process-local state durable. Do not claim host-loss protection from Kafka retention alone.\nUnverified: No deployment choice is settled. The actor-runtime choice is separate.\nNext:       Read fp CHAT-pphwooqm and the merged Stage 1 spec before any work.\nPointers:   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-07-domain-command-bus-design.md, fp CHAT-pphwooqm, PR #201.\n"}
